According to a report by Intel Market Research, the global Automotive Artificial Intelligence Software market was valued at USD 5.5 billion in 2025 and is projected to grow from USD 7.2 billion in 2026 to USD 60 billion by 2034, registering an impressive CAGR of 30.2% during the forecast period. The market is witnessing remarkable expansion as artificial intelligence becomes the foundation of next-generation vehicles, enabling advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS), autonomous driving capabilities, predictive maintenance, intelligent human-machine interfaces, and software-defined vehicle architectures. Growing investments in electric vehicles (EVs), autonomous mobility, edge computing, and connected transportation ecosystems are significantly accelerating the adoption of automotive AI software across the global automotive industry.
